WEBVTT

00:02:59.273 --> 00:03:01.548
before retracing my footprints home,

00:03:01.572 --> 00:03:03.850
finally putting my hometown on the map.

00:03:04.414 --> 00:03:07.354
And yet, much of the region
remains all but invisible

00:03:07.378 --> 00:03:09.712
on some of the most widely used
mapping platforms.

00:03:10.976 --> 00:03:12.710
Beyond navigation,

00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:15.101
maps are a proxy for what we care about.

00:03:15.125 --> 00:03:17.667
They tell us about the quality
of the air we breathe,

00:03:17.691 --> 00:03:20.034
the potential for
renewable energy solutions

00:03:20.058 --> 00:03:21.915
and the safety of our streets.

00:03:21.939 --> 00:03:24.415
These lines retrace
the journeys we've taken.

00:03:24.439 --> 00:03:27.463
In a sense, maps
are a form of storytelling.

00:03:27.982 --> 00:03:31.594
When you look at the state of mapping
on the African continent today,